changes_a_127_ruling:
Point 3's 'partly right' verdict and ruling stand in direction. Three amendments are narrowed and extended.

KS-O17 needs five additions:
- a lookup-time entry roster, so 'existed at the watermark' is mechanical;
- a specified classifier (content terms, stop list, placeholders excluded, strict typo rule, precedence, filtered and symptom_differs classes);
- definitions of same, related and new;
- a blind reviewer re-check with a fixture;
- a mechanical rephrase-then-hit writer.
It also needs rebuild and restore re-ingestion or rollup fallbacks, so the view never reads 0 for an unknown.

KS-O18 is changed: 'k ≥ 3 … reported as k of n' becomes a windowed rule with an exact binomial bound over examined lookups whose answer existed. The claim that it is 'numerically the same as v1.2's 5 % of 50' is withdrawn, since v1.2 used a lookup denominator over a sliding 50-lookup window. The text records that the trigger is not expected to fire before KS-9.

KS-O19 is narrowed: the dense-only candidate is computed after the step-2 filters; not_when and dead-end handling are specified; and KS-F8's template requirement extends to candidates that reach applies on necessary_condition entries. The carve-out recovers misses only to candidate, and past the gate only for entries with a runnable check.
